@using BrainHarbor.Web.Models
@inject BrainHarbor.Web.Feed.CardImages CardImages
@model FeedCard

@*
    One feed card (WI-109), identical on the homepage and /research.

    Anatomy: hero (content-matched photo + the readiness dial) → badge → title
    → hook → tags + date · source.

    The 2026-08-15 homepage handoff specified a plainer card with neither the
    photo nor the dial. Dan's call, 2026-08-15, after seeing both live: the
    /research card is the better one, and the homepage should match it. The dial
    is the reason — "how far along the ready scale a finding is" is information
    the homepage was missing, and it is the thing the badge does NOT say. The
    badge is about how well tested the evidence is; the dial is about how close
    it is to something a patient can actually get.

    See docs/design/README.md, which records this as a deliberate deviation so
    nobody later "restores" the handoff version.
*@
<li class="card">
    @BrainHarbor.Web.Feed.CardArt.Hero(Model, CardImages.UrlFor(Model))
    <partial name="_StageBadge" model="StageBadge.For(Model.Stage)" />
    <h3><a href="@Model.Url">@Model.Title</a></h3>
    <p class="card__hook">@Model.Hook</p>
    <p class="card__meta">
        @* Topic chips stay: tumor type is how a patient finds the item that is
           actually about them. *@
        @foreach (var tag in Model.Tags)
        {
            <span class="tag">@tag</span>
        }
        <span>@Model.DateText · @Model.Source</span>
    </p>
</li>
